-- חוזר הממונה על השכר 2015-1-8 — תוספת מעונות (זכויות הוריות), עדכון התוספת (18.1.2015)
-- The Wage Controller updates the monthly childcare supplement (parental
-- rights) for a child up to age 5, under clause 11 of the framework
-- agreement of 12.1.2011, and prints the new amounts.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `תוספת מעונות (זכויות הוריות), עדכון התוספת 2015-1-8`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 The letterhead, the date, the circular's number, the addressee (the Deputy Accountant-General) and the subject line; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p2 The letterhead's address line; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p3 The Hebrew date; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p4 The date, 18.1.2015; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p5 The circular's number, הע-2015-1-8; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p6 The addressee; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p7 The subject line; no rule.

@desc A child for whom the childcare supplement is claimed, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `child for the childcare supplement` HAS
    `up to age 5`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc the child is "עד גיל 5", the age the circular names; who that is, and who may claim, is clause 11 of the framework agreement of 12.1.2011, which this circular does not restate
    `place among the children`      IS A NUMBER  @desc 1 for "ילד אחד / ילד ראשון" (an only or first child), 2 for "ילד שני" (a second child), counted as clause 11 of the framework agreement counts them

§§ `The update`

-- The date the update takes effect, as printed ("החל מיום 1.1.15").
@ref akn:hc_1/p9
`the update takes effect` MEANS Date 1 1 2015

§§ `1–2 The amounts`

@ref akn:hc_1__para_1
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly amount for an only or first child` IS 316

@ref akn:hc_1__para_2
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly amount for a second child` IS 212

-- The circular prints amounts for an only or first child and for a second
-- child, and nothing for any other: whether a third child is paid for is
-- not this circular's question, so it gives NOTHING there rather than a
-- zero it does not print.
@export default The monthly childcare supplement (in shekels) this update sets for a child, from the date it takes effect
@ref akn:hc_1/p9
GIVEN c       IS A `child for the childcare supplement` @desc the child
      `month` IS A DATE                                @desc a day in the month the supplement is for
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` c `month` IS
    BRANCH IF `month` LESS THAN `the update takes effect` THEN NOTHING
           IF (NOT c's `up to age 5`)                    THEN NOTHING
           IF c's `place among the children` EQUALS 1   THEN JUST `the monthly amount for an only or first child`
           IF c's `place among the children` EQUALS 2   THEN JUST `the monthly amount for a second child`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Payment`

DECLARE `childcare supplement action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the childcare supplement` HAS `childcare amount paid` IS A NUMBER

-- From the date it takes effect the employers pay the supplement at the
-- updated amount. The circular sets a monthly amount ("לחודש") and no
-- payment date; time is counted in months from the start of the month the
-- supplement is for, and the supplement is read as due within that month.
@ref akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1__para_1 akn:hc_1__para_2
GIVEN c       IS A `child for the childcare supplement`
      `month` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `childcare supplement action`
DECIDE `the employer pays the updated supplement` c `month` IS
    CONSIDER `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` c `month`
    WHEN JUST due THEN
        PARTY `the employer`
        MUST  `pay the childcare supplement` paid
              PROVIDED paid AT LEAST due
        WITHIN 1
        LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "the childcare supplement was not paid at the updated amount for the month"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FULFILLED

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off (the Wage Controller), the copy to the Civil Service Commissioner, the internal number and the letterhead's footer; no rule.

§§ `Findings`

-- F-2015-01_sachar_2015-1-8_maonot-a. The reference line names the
-- circular this update continues as הע-2014-1-9. The update of the same
-- supplement for 2014 — the amounts this circular moves on from (317 and
-- 212, from 1.1.14) — is circular הע-2014-1-3 of 19.1.2014 (corpus
-- circulars-sachar/2014-01_sachar_2014-1-3_maonot, its own number line).
-- That number is used here only as evidence, never as a rule.
@ref akn:hc_1/p8
`the circular this update names as its predecessor` MEANS "2014-1-9"

`the number of the 2014 update of the supplement` MEANS "2014-1-3"

`the reference line names a circular that is not the 2014 update` MEANS
    NOT (`the circular this update names as its predecessor` EQUALS `the number of the 2014 update of the supplement`)
#ASSERT `the reference line names a circular that is not the 2014 update`

§§ `Examples`

`an only child of three` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 1

`a second child of two` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 2

`a third child of one` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS TRUE
        `place among the children` IS 3

`a first child of seven` MEANS
    `child for the childcare supplement` WITH
        `up to age 5`              IS FALSE
        `place among the children` IS 1

#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `an only child of three` (Date 1 1 2015) EQUALS JUST 316
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a second child of two` (Date 15 3 2015) EQUALS JUST 212
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `an only child of three` (Date 31 12 2014) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a third child of one` (Date 15 3 2015) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the monthly childcare supplement under this update` `a first child of seven` (Date 15 3 2015) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Paid in full within the month, the obligation is fulfilled; paid short,
-- it is still owed.
#TRACE `the employer pays the updated supplement` `an only child of three` (Date 15 3 2015) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the childcare supplement` 316 AT 0
#TRACE `the employer pays the updated supplement` `an only child of three` (Date 15 3 2015) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the childcare supplement` 300 AT 0
